{#- The front door (targum-internal#69, 2026-09-16).

    The one page a stranger meets. It is not the desk and not a reader: it carries its
    own bar, its own foot, and the four things on it that move — the vowel switches, the
    reading modes, the box's Start and the waitlist's form — are the product doing what
    the page says it does rather than a picture of it.

    Everything it draws is baked in. No script, stylesheet, font or image comes off the
    network, which is the reader's rule (§11) and holds here for the same reason: the
    first page anybody sees should not be a page that phones somebody else first.

    The waitlist's form is a plain post to `/waitlist`, and works with JavaScript off.
    `landing.js` only makes the demos move. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{#- The alternates moved into `_public_head.html.j2` on 2026-09-22, when the text pages
    and the weekly began declaring theirs too. That file's own header says a head kept in
    four copies is four copies that drift, and this was the copy. -#}
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('landing.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{#- The Torah's own face, beside the modern one: the ta'amim are boxes without it. -#}
{{ scripture_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="landing">
<a class="skip" href="#top">{{ t("landing.page.skip-to-the-page", "Skip to the page") }}</a>
{% with bar_class = 'bar', home = '', here = '/' %}{% include '_front_bar.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

<main id="top">
  <div class="col top">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="headline">
        <h1>{{ t("landing.page.learn-modern-and-biblical-hebrew-from-videos-podcasts", "Learn modern and biblical Hebrew from videos, podcasts and books.") }}</h1>
          <p class="lede">{{ t("landing.page.you-learn-hebrew-by-understanding-it-so-everything", "You learn Hebrew by understanding it. So everything here arrives ready to read: vowels (nikkud) on every word, English beside every line, and an explanation for any word you tap.") }}</p>
        {#- Try the door (targum-internal#399): paste a link and be told what it is, in
            the Add box's own sentence. A plain post, so it works with JavaScript off;
            the answer comes back on this page. Nothing is built and nothing is spent,
            and no percentage is shown: "you know X%" needs a record, and getting one
            is the reason to join (2026-09-30). -#}
        <div class="try" id="try">
          <form class="try-form" method="post" action="/try{% if asked %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}#try">
            <label class="field">
              <input type="url" name="link" required inputmode="url" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{{ t("landing.try.placeholder", "Paste a link to anything in Hebrew") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.try.label", "A link to try") }}"{% if tried and tried.link %} value="{{ tried.link }}"{% endif %}>
              <button class="btn tonal" type="submit">{{ t("landing.try.button", "Try it") }}</button>
            </label>
          </form>
          {%- if tried %}
          <div class="tried" role="status">
            {%- if tried.refused %}
            <p class="tried-what">{{ tried.refused }}</p>
            {%- else %}
            <p class="tried-what">
              {%- if tried.door == 'youtube' %}{{ t("landing.try.youtube", "That’s a YouTube video") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'instagram' %}{{ t("landing.try.instagram", "That’s an Instagram reel") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'instagram-post' %}{{ t("landing.try.instagram-post", "That’s an Instagram post") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'tiktok' %}{{ t("landing.try.tiktok", "That’s a TikTok video") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'facebook' %}{{ t("landing.try.facebook", "That’s a Facebook video") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'x' %}{{ t("landing.try.x", "That’s a post on X") }}
              {%- elif tried.door == 'podcast' %}{{ t("landing.try.podcast", "That’s a podcast episode") }}
              {%- else %}{{ t("landing.try.page", "That’s a page from {site}", site=tried.site) }}{% endif %}
              {%- if tried.minutes %}, {{ tn("landing.try.minutes", tried.minutes, "{n} minute", "{n} minutes") }}{% endif %}
              {%- if tried.sentences %}, {{ tn("landing.try.sentences", tried.sentences, "{n} sentence", "{n} sentences") }}{% endif %}
              {%- if tried.subtitles %}, {{ t("landing.try.subtitles", "Hebrew subtitles written by a person") }}{% endif %}.
              {%- if tried.wait %} {{ tried.wait }}{% endif %}</p>
            {%- if tried.title %}
            <p class="tried-title" dir="auto">{{ tried.title }}</p>
            {%- endif %}
            <p class="tried-keep">{{ t("landing.try.keep", "Join to keep it. When your turn comes, it’ll be waiting for you, ready to learn from.") }}</p>
            {% with note = false, link = tried.link %}{% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
            {%- endif %}
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
        {#- One call to action in the hero, the box (David, 2026-10-02): its answer carries
            the waitlist, and the bar keeps Join the waitlist. Under it, only the reasons. -#}
        <ul class="facts">
          {#- The live page's own four (David, 2026-10-02). Claude and ChatGPT are met in
              "Talk to targum", not here (design.md §12). -#}
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.start-at-any-level", "Start at any level") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.upload-any-text-or-media", "Upload any text or media") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.hundreds-of-free-texts-and-videos", "Hundreds of free texts and videos") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.no-credit-card-required", "No credit card required") }}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- The word card stands beside the headline (David, 2026-10-02), so the hero and the
        reader under it read as one composition; the reader runs the full width below.
        On a phone it follows the reader instead. -#}
    <aside class="card" id="card" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.word-card", "Word card") }}"></aside>
    <p class="sr-only" id="cardSaid" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="showcase">
      <article class="reader" id="reader" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.example-a-cooking-video-in-the-reader", "Example: a cooking video in the reader") }}">
        <div class="reader-head">
          <div>
            <p class="reader-title">{{ t("landing.page.shakshuka-in-ten-minutes", "Shakshuka in ten minutes") }}</p>
            <p class="reader-meta">{{ t("landing.page.a-cooking-video-10-minutes-you-know-80", "A cooking video · 10 minutes · you know 80% of the words here") }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="keys">
            <button class="btn tonal small" id="vowels" type="button" aria-pressed="true">{{ t("landing.page.vowels", "Vowels") }}</button>
            <button class="btn tonal small" id="pin" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="3" width="12" height="10" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><rect x="8.5" y="4.5" width="4" height="3" rx="0.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
              <span id="pinWord">{{ t("landing.page.corner", "Corner") }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage" id="stage">
          <canvas id="film" width="960" height="432" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
          <div class="captions" id="captions" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="c-he" id="capHe"></p>
            <p class="c-en" id="capEn"></p>
          </div>
          <button class="stage-tap" id="stageTap" type="button" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.play-or-pause-the-video", "Play or pause the video") }}">
            <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 3v10l8-5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="strip">
          <button class="play" id="play" type="button" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.play", "Play") }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" id="playGlyph"><path d="M5 3v10l8-5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          </button>
          <span class="clock tnum" id="clock">2:20 / 10:12</span>
          <span class="track" id="track" role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.position", "Position") }}" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="18" aria-valuenow="10"><i id="fill"></i></span>
          <button class="rate" id="rate" type="button" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.speed", "Speed") }}">1×</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lines" id="lines"></div>
        <div class="reader-foot">
          <span class="legend"><i class="l-learning"></i>{{ t("landing.page.working-on-it", "working on it") }}</span>
          <span class="legend"><i class="l-new"></i>{{ t("landing.page.new-to-you", "new to you") }}</span>
          <span>{{ t("landing.page.tap-any-word-or-a-time-to-hear", "Tap any word, or a time to hear the line again.") }}</span>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="part" id="own">
    <div class="col split">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.your-own-hebrew", "Your own Hebrew") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.if-it-s-in-hebrew-you-can-learn", "If it’s in Hebrew, you can learn from it here.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.paste-a-link-or-drop-a-file-whatever", "Paste a link or drop a file. Recordings are written out word by word and timed to the voice, so each word lights up as it’s said.") }}</p>
      </div>
      {#- What the box gives back once you're in (2026-10-02): the one sentence about the
          link, how much of it you already know, and when it's ready. Drawn, because a
          stranger has no record to measure against; the box in the hero is the live one. -#}
      <figure class="example" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.example-what-you-d-see", "Example: what you’d see once you’re in") }}">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.what-you-d-see", "What you’d see") }}</p>
        <div class="example-card">
          <span class="thumb" aria-hidden="true"><span class="len tnum">9:04</span></span>
          <div class="example-body">
            <p class="example-what">{{ t("landing.page.that-s-a-youtube-video-9-minutes", "That’s a YouTube video, 9 minutes, Hebrew subtitles written by a person.") }}</p>
            <p class="example-title">{{ t("landing.page.sabich-step-by-step", "Sabich, step by step") }}</p>
            <p class="example-known"><b class="tnum">80%</b> {{ t("landing.page.of-it-you-already-know", "of it you already know") }}</p>
            <span class="meter"><i class="p80"></i></span>
            <p class="example-wait">{{ t("landing.page.ready-in-about-4-minutes", "Ready in about 4 minutes.") }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
        {#- Where the Hebrew comes from, each drawn as what it looks like (2026-10-01): the
            page's one inverted block, beside the box that takes it. -#}
        <div class="media bring">
          <ul class="media-grid eight">
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis"><div class="v-frame"></div><div class="v-cap"><span class="he">עַכְשָׁיו שׁוֹבְרִים אֶת הַבֵּיצִים</span><span>{{ t("landing.page.now-crack-the-eggs", "Now crack the eggs") }}</span></div></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.a-youtube-link-or-a-video-file", "A YouTube link or a video file") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis tall-row"><span class="tall"><span class="v-frame"></span><span class="t-cap he">יַאלְלָה, בּוֹאוּ</span></span><span class="tall"><span class="v-frame b"></span><span class="t-cap he">אֵיזֶה יוֹפִי</span></span><span class="tall"><span class="v-frame c"></span><span class="t-cap he">תִּרְאוּ אֶת זֶה</span></span></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.reels-shorts-tiktoks-and-facebook-videos", "Reels, Shorts, TikToks and Facebook videos") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis"><div class="wave" id="bringWave"></div><span class="wave-clock tnum">18:40 / 31:06</span></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.a-podcast", "A podcast") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis"><div class="note-bubble"><span class="dot"></span><span class="mini" id="bringMini"></span><span class="len tnum">0:47</span></div><p class="note-line">הֵי, רָאִיתָ אֶת הַהוֹדָעָה שֶׁשָּׁלַחְתִּי?</p></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.a-voice-note", "A voice note") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis post-vis"><span class="who"><b class="dot"></b><b class="name">@kan_news</b></span><p class="he">הַיּוֹם בָּעֶרֶב: סִדְרָה חֲדָשָׁה לְכָל הַמִּשְׁפָּחָה</p></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.posts-from-x", "Posts from X") }}{% if not x_open %}<span class="soon"> {{ t("landing.page.soon", "soon") }}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis chat-vis"><p class="he in">סַבְתָּא, אֵיךְ עוֹשִׂים שַׁקְשׁוּקָה?</p><p class="he out">רַק עַגְבָנִיּוֹת טוֹבוֹת, בָּצָל וְשׁוּם.</p></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.a-whatsapp-or-telegram-chat", "A WhatsApp or Telegram chat") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis news-vis"><p class="he head">הַגֶּשֶׁם חוֹזֵר בְּסוֹף הַשָּׁבוּעַ</p><p class="he">הַתַּחֲזִית: גְּשָׁמִים בַּצָּפוֹן וּבַמֶּרְכָּז, וְקַר יוֹתֵר בַּלַּיְלָה.</p></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.news-and-articles-from-any-site", "News and articles, from any site") }}</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="m-tile">
              <div class="m-vis page-vis"><span class="sheet-p"><i></i><i></i><i class="s"></i><i></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="sheet-p back"><i></i><i class="s"></i><i></i></span></div>
              <h3>{{ t("landing.page.a-photo-of-a-letter-a-form-a-sign", "A photo of a letter, a form or a sign") }}</h3>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="how">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.how-you-learn", "How you learn") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.learn-a-little-hebrew-every-day-from-things", "Learn a little Hebrew every day, from things you’d choose anyway.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.no-drills-and-no-textbook-dialogues-pick-a", "Pick a video, a podcast or a chapter, and targum turns it into a lesson built on the words you already know.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="how">
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("landing.page.pick-something-just-past-what-you-know", "Pick something just past what you know") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("landing.page.the-library-is-sorted-by-the-words-you", "We compare every word in a text with the words you know, so you see how much you’ll understand before you start.") }}</p>
          <div class="how-vis">
            <div class="how-row"><span>{{ t("landing.page.shakshuka-in-ten-minutes", "Shakshuka in ten minutes") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p80"></i></span></div>
            <div class="how-row"><span>{{ t("landing.page.this-week-s-news-easy", "This week’s news · easy") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p90"></i></span></div>
            <div class="how-row"><span>{{ t("landing.page.homemade-hummus-step-by-step", "Homemade hummus, step by step") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p70"></i></span></div>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("landing.page.tap-any-word", "Tap any word") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("landing.page.tap-any-word-said", "Each word comes with its dictionary form, root and binyan. Missing vowels are filled in, and each one we add is marked.") }}</p>
          {#- "Every word" folded in here (2026-10-01): the reader at the top already shows
              a whole card, so this shows the one thing it cannot, the vowels going. -#}
          <div class="how-vis center">
            <p class="he how-word vs-word" id="vsRecipe"></p>
            <span class="how-gloss">{{ t("landing.page.for-it-to-heat-up", "for it to heat up") }}</span>
            <span class="how-root"><bdi>hitpa’el</bdi> · <span class="he">ח־מ־ם</span></span>
            <button class="switch" id="swVowels" type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="true"><span class="knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ t("landing.page.vowels", "Vowels") }}</button>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("landing.page.watch-your-hebrew-grow", "Watch your Hebrew grow") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("landing.page.every-word-you-learn-is-counted-and-moves", "Every word you learn is counted and moves you up the ulpan ladder, so you can see how far you’ve come.") }}</p>
          <div class="how-vis">
            <div class="how-count"><span class="v">2,140</span><span>{{ t("landing.page.words-known", "words known ·") }} <span class="he">ב</span> {{ t("landing.page.bet", "bet") }}</span></div>
            <div class="how-bars"><i class="h30 on"></i><i class="h42 on"></i><i class="h54 part"></i><i class="h66"></i><i class="h78"></i><i class="h90"></i></div>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="talk">
    <div class="col split">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.ask-anything-and-practise-talking-while-you-do", "Ask anything, and practise talking while you do.") }}</h2>
        {#- Three plain sentences rather than two paragraphs or a row of icons
            (2026-10-02): what you do, what comes back, and where else it works. The last
            is the connector, said lightly (design.md §12, 2026-09-28). -#}
        <ul class="talk-points">
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.talk.write", "Write in Hebrew or English.") }} {{ t("landing.page.talk.write.said", "targum answers in simple Hebrew, with the English underneath.") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.talk.fix", "When you slip,") }} {{ t("landing.page.talk.fix.said", "it shows you the right sentence and why.") }}</li>
          {%- if connector_is_open() %}
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.talk.claude", "It works in Claude and ChatGPT too.") }} {{ t("landing.page.talk.claude.said", "Ask what to read next, and it answers from the words you know.") }} <a href="/connect">{{ t("landing.page.see-how-to-connect", "See how to connect") }}</a></li>
          {%- endif %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      {#- The conversation on a phone (2026-10-02), the way it is mostly had. A picture of
          a device, so its corners are cut by `clip-path`: the radius scale is for the
          interface, and a phone's corners are far rounder than any step on it. -#}
      <figure class="talk-phone">
        <div class="phone">
          <div class="screen">
            <span class="island" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="app-bar" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="20 12 56 72"><rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect><rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect></svg>
              targum
            </div>
            {#- Drawn as /chat draws it (design.md §9; targum-internal#247): who said a line
                is told by where it stands, the reader's set in from the start and targum's
                from the end, the same ink on both, never two colours of bubble. -#}
            <ol class="ct-turns" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.example-conversation", "Example conversation") }}">
              <li class="ct-turn me">
                <span class="ct-who">{{ t("landing.page.you", "You") }}</span>
                <p class="ct-he">השקשוקה שלי היה טעים</p>
              </li>
              <li class="ct-turn them">
                <span class="ct-who">targum</span>
                <div class="ct-pair ct-recast">
                  <span class="ct-tag">{{ t("landing.page.corrected", "Corrected") }}</span>
                  <p class="ct-he">הַשַּׁקְשׁוּקָה שֶׁלִּי <span class="fix">הָיְתָה</span> <span class="fix">טְעִימָה</span>.</p>
                  <p class="ct-en">{{ t("landing.page.my-shakshuka-was-delicious", "My shakshuka was delicious.") }}</p>
                  <button class="fold" id="whyFold" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="why">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                    {{ t("landing.page.why", "Why") }}
                  </button>
                  <p class="ct-why" id="why" hidden><span class="he">שַׁקְשׁוּקָה</span> {{ t("landing.page.is-feminine-so-the-verb-and-the-adjective", "is feminine, so the verb and the adjective are too.") }}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ct-pair">
                  <p class="ct-he">נִשְׁמָע טָעִים. יֵשׁ לָנוּ סִרְטוֹן עַל חוּמוּס בֵּיתִי. רוֹצֶה לִרְאוֹת?</p>
                  <p class="ct-en">{{ t("landing.page.sounds-delicious-we-have-a-video-on-homemade", "Sounds delicious. We have a video on homemade hummus. Want to watch it?") }}</p>
                </div>
                <a class="btn cta small door" href="#reader">{{ t("landing.page.open-homemade-hummus", "Open Homemade hummus") }}</a>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <div class="ct-sum tnum">
              <span>{{ t("landing.page.2-new-words-on-your-list", "2 new words on your list") }}</span>
              <a href="#reader">{{ t("landing.page.keep-as-a-text", "Keep as a text") }}</a>
            </div>
            <div class="composer" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>{{ t("chat.page.write-in-hebrew-or-english", "Write in Hebrew or English") }}</span>
              <span class="send"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 13V3M3.5 7.5 8 3l4.5 4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="part" id="library">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.the-library", "The library") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.nearly-500-texts-and-videos-to-learn-from", "Nearly 500 texts and videos to learn from, free.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.this-week-s-news-at-three-levels-videos", "This week’s news at three levels, graded stories, Bialik and the whole Tanakh, many with a published translation set beside the Hebrew sentence by sentence.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="shelf">
        <div class="book"><span class="reg">{{ t("landing.page.video", "Video") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.shakshuka-in-ten-minutes", "Shakshuka in ten minutes") }}</span><span class="k tnum">{{ t("landing.page.80-of-words-known", "80% of words known") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p80"></i></span></div>
        <div class="book"><span class="reg">{{ t("landing.page.modern", "Modern") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.this-week-s-news-easy", "This week’s news · easy") }}</span><span class="k tnum">{{ t("landing.page.90-of-words-known", "90% of words known") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p90"></i></span></div>
        <div class="book"><span class="reg">{{ t("landing.page.revival", "Revival") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.bialik", "Bialik ·") }} <span class="he">הַכְנִיסִינִי</span></span><span class="k tnum">{{ t("landing.page.60-of-words-known", "60% of words known") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p60"></i></span></div>
        <div class="book"><span class="reg">{{ t("landing.page.biblical", "Biblical") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.genesis-1-with-onkelos", "Genesis 1, with Onkelos") }}</span><span class="k tnum">{{ t("landing.page.70-of-words-known", "70% of words known") }}</span><span class="meter"><i class="p70"></i></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {#- The Torah is in the library, so it is drawn there (2026-10-01): the shelf, then
        Genesis as its centrepiece, rather than a part of its own. -#}
    <div class="col split torah-in" id="torah">
      <div class="part-head">
        <h3>{{ t("landing.page.genesis-with-its-chanting-marks-and-onkelos-beside", "Genesis with its chanting marks, and Onkelos beside it.") }}</h3>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.the-hebrew-with-its-chanting-marks-an-english", "The Hebrew with its chanting marks, an English translation under every verse, and Targum Onkelos whenever you want the Aramaic.") }}</p>
        <ul class="points">
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.chanting-marks-on-or-off", "Chanting marks on or off.") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.the-weekly-portion-read-aloud", "The weekly portion chanted, each word lit as it’s sung.") }}</li>
          <li>{{ t("landing.page.daniel-and-ezra-s-aramaic-chapters-on-a", "Daniel and Ezra’s Aramaic chapters, on a list of their own.") }}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <article class="sheet torah" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.example-genesis-1-1-3", "Example: Genesis 1:1–3") }}">
        <div class="sheet-head">
          <div>
            <p class="sheet-title">{{ t("landing.page.genesis-1-bereshit", "Genesis 1 · Bereshit") }}</p>
            <p class="sheet-meta" id="torahMeta">{{ t("landing.page.hebrew-english", "Hebrew · English") }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.how-to-read", "How to read") }}">
            <button type="button" data-mode="read" aria-pressed="true">{{ t("landing.page.read", "Read") }}</button>
            <button type="button" data-mode="verse" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("landing.page.by-verse", "By verse") }}</button>
            <button type="button" data-mode="aliyah" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("landing.page.by-aliyah", "By aliyah") }}</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="verses"></div>
        <div class="torah-foot" id="torahFoot" hidden></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="questions">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.questions", "Questions") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.before-you-join", "Before you join.") }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.when-does-it-open", "When does it open?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-rather-than", "We’re opening in small groups. Join the waitlist and we’ll email you when your turn comes.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-targum-for-me", "Is targum for me?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.if-you-re-learning-hebrew-and-know-the", "If you’re learning Hebrew and know the alphabet, yes: whether you’re fresh out of an ulpan, a year into an app, studying for a degree or keeping up with the weekly portion. The library is sorted by the words you already know, so there’s always something you can learn from.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.does-it-replace-a-course", "Does it replace a course?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.it-s-the-other-half-of-one-a", "It’s the other half of one. A course teaches you the rules; targum gives you real Hebrew to practise them on, every day, and keeps count of every word you learn.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.biblical-or-modern", "Biblical or modern?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.both-on-one-list-a-word-you-learn", "Both, on one list. A word you learn in Genesis is already yours when it turns up in the news.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.what-will-it-cost", "What will it cost?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.the-library-is-free-to-read-and-stays", "The library is free to read and stays free. There’ll be a paid plan for reading your own Hebrew: the videos, podcasts and books you bring us.") }}</p></details>
        {%- if connector_is_open() %}
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.can-i-use-it-in-claude-or-chatgpt", "Can I use it in Claude or ChatGPT?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.yes-connect-targum-and-your-ai-talks", "Yes. Connect targum and your AI talks to you in Hebrew built from the words you know, and shows you how to fix each mistake.") }} <a href="/connect">{{ t("landing.page.see-how-to-connect", "See how to connect") }}</a></p></details>
        {%- endif %}
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-what-i-bring-private", "Is what I bring private?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.yes-what-you-bring-is-yours-and-we", "Yes. What you bring is yours, and we never train a model on it.") }}</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- The page's ending, not a fourth example: centred on the page itself, with no paper
      under it, so the only raised sheets on the landing are the product's (§8, one
      raised layer per view; David, 2026-10-02). -#}
  <section class="part" id="join">
    <div class="col join-end">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.the-waitlist", "The waitlist") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.be-among-the-first-to-learn-hebrew-this", "Be among the first to learn Hebrew this way.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-leave-your", "We’re opening in small groups. Leave your email and we’ll tell you when it’s your turn.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="join-body">
        {% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}
        <p class="join-note">{{ t("landing.page.free-to-start-with-the-whole-library-open", "Free to start, with the whole library open.") }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


</main>

{% with signin = true %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('landing.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
